des/seed1583749884/2/des.md:80:  - 在重叠交叉处，可见颜色属于上层框。由此构建从底到顶的颜色分层顺序。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/des.md:81:  - 创建输出：按照从最底层到最顶层的顺序，将颜色绘制为同心嵌套的矩形框。最底层颜色作为最外层框，最顶层颜色作为最内层框。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/des.md:82:  - 输出尺寸为 (2K-1) x (2K-1)，其中 K 是颜色数。每层框的厚度为一像素。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/des.md:83:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/des.md:84:- `Key insight`：输出不是输入的裁剪，而是对遮挡关系图的重新渲染；解题者需要先通过交叉点处的可见性推断分层顺序，再理解嵌套框的构建规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/des.md:85:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:1:你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:3:每个参考题描述包含：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:4:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8886d717\" lines=\"43-63\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:12:Repair markers embedded in the main object and copy the remaining markers one pixel toward the solid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:14:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:15:- A mostly background grid contains one solid non-background edge line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:16:- Apart from that edge and the background, there is one large main object\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:17:  color and a smaller marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:18:- Each marker is either embedded in the main object, touching it on at\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:19:  least three 4-neighbor sides, or isolated on the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:20:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:21:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:22:- Embedded markers are recolored to the main object color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:23:- Isolated background markers remain in place and also paint the adjacent\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:24:  background pixel in the direction of the solid edge line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:25:- All other pixels are unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:26:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:27:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:28:The full edge line is a direction cue: it tells which way the background\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:29:markers extend, while markers surrounded by the main object are simply\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:30:defects to be filled.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:31:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:32:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:33:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:34:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88bcf3b4\" lines=\"229-241\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:35:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:36:Swing an irregular line segment around a nearby obstacle sprite, preserving its pixel count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:37:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:38:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:39:- bg, bar color (straight lines perpendicular to the grid edge, one end on the border), segment color (irregular stroke attached to bar's inner endpoint), obstacle color (sprite near the bar terminal).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:40:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:41:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:42:- Each bar is perpendicular to the edge it touches; its inner (terminal) endpoint has an attached irregular segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:43:- The segment detaches and re-routes: it travels from the terminal toward the nearest obstacle, hugs the obstacle's boundary, then exits at a 45° diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:44:- Total painted pixels equal the original segment length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:45:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:46:Key insight: The segment behaves like a rope swung around the obstacle — attach at the nearest point, trace the skin, exit diagonally, conserving length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:47:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:48:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:49:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:50:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b0039139\" lines=\"29-44\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:51:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:52:Recolor a cropped template and repeat it according to a component-count stencil.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:53:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:54:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:55:- Solid blue (1) separator rows or columns split the grid into four sections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:56:- Section 1 is a black-background shape template; section 2 is a component-count stencil.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:57:- Sections 3 and 4 are solid color swatches for output foreground and background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:58:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:59:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:60:- Crop section 1 to the bbox of its non-black pixels and recolor it with the two swatches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:61:- Count 4-connected non-black components in section 2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:62:- Repeat the recolored crop that many times, inserting one background-colored row/column between copies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:63:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:64:Key insight: The second section encodes only the repeat count; the output orientation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:65:is inherited from whether the input separators are columns or rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:66:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:67:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:68:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:69:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"68bc2e87\" lines=\"46-60\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:70:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:71:Recover the bottom-to-top stacking order of overlaid rectangular color frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:72:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:73:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:74:- The background is one color, and every foreground color is a one-cell-thick rectangular frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:75:- Overlapping frame pixels show only the color of the frame that is highest at that location.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:76:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:77:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:78:- Reconstruct each frame as the border of the bounding box of its visible pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:79:- At every cell covered by multiple reconstructed frames, the visible frame color is above the other frames covering that cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:80:- Return the unique bottom-to-top order of frame colors as a single-column grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:81:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:82:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:83:The hidden parts of each frame do not need to be seen directly; the visible pixels reveal the full frame bbox, and overlap cells reveal the layer constraints.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:84:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:85:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:86:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:87:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aaef0977\" lines=\"25-41\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:88:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:89:Replace an orange canvas with concentric Manhattan-distance color rings centered on the lone marker pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:90:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:91:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:92:- The grid is an orange background with exactly one non-orange marker pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:93:- The marker color is one of the colors in the fixed non-orange ring cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:94:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:95:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:96:- The marker location is distance 0 and keeps the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:97:- Each step of Manhattan distance away from the marker advances one position\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:98:  through the cycle green, yellow, black, grey, red, teal, maroon, pink, blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:99:- Fill every pixel of the original grid by this distance-indexed cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:100:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:101:Key insight: The output is not copied from existing objects; it is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:102:distance field around the single marker, colored by a cyclic palette that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:103:excludes the orange background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:104:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:105:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:106:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:107:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"de809cff\" lines=\"86-103\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:108:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:109:Turn black dents in two colored regions into marked opposite-color patches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:110:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:111:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:112:- Black background with two large foreground colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:113:- The large regions contain small black dents and a few one-cell color specks\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:114:  or protrusions along region boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:115:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:116:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:117:- Locally clean the two foreground regions: isolated specks become black, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:118:  one-cell protrusions surrounded by the other region take that region's color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:119:- Each original black dent whose cleaned 3x3 neighborhood is mostly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:120:  foreground color becomes the center of a 3x3 patch in the opposite color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:121:- The dent center itself is recolored teal (8).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:122:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:123:Key insight: The teal pixels mark the original black defects; the surrounding\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:124:3x3 patch uses the other foreground color, after first removing boundary noise.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:125:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:126:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:127:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:128:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ac0c2ac3\" lines=\"7-19\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:129:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:130:Fill each centered square ring with the color of the marker at that ring distance.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:131:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:132:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:133:The input is an odd square grid with a dominant background color and one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:134:non-background marker for every Chebyshev distance from the grid center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:135:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:136:The output replaces the background with concentric square rings centered on\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:137:the middle cell; every cell at distance d from the center takes the color of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:138:the unique marker whose distance from the center is d.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:139:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:140:The scattered markers are not objects to move; their Chebyshev distances\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:141:form a palette for the centered square rings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:142:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:143:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:144:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:145:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9b30e358\" lines=\"9-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:146:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:147:Repeat the bottom foreground motif upward until it fills the whole grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:148:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:149:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:150:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:151:- The only foreground pixels occupy a contiguous block of rows at the bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:152:- That bottom block is the complete vertical motif, including its background cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:153:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:154:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:155:- Copy the bottom motif rows repeatedly upward across the full grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:156:- Preserve horizontal alignment and vertical phase: the original first motif row remains at its input row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:157:- The output shape is unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:158:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:159:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:160:The blank rows above the bottom foreground block are missing repetitions of the same row motif, not empty space.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:161:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:162:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:163:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:164:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b7256dcd\" lines=\"18-32\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:165:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:166:Transfer each colored marker to its adjacent neutral mask component, then erase the markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:167:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:168:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:169:- The background is the most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:170:- The neutral mask color is the unique most frequent foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:171:- Other foreground colors are marker pixels that may touch neutral 4-connected mask components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:172:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:173:- Remove every marker pixel by recoloring it to the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:174:- For each 4-connected neutral mask component, find marker colors touching it by edge adjacency.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:175:- If a component touches one marker color, recolor the whole neutral component to that marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:176:- If a component touches no marker color, leave it neutral.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:177:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:178:- Marker pixels label neighboring neutral regions but are not part of the final colored objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:179:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:180:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:181:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:182:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3ad05f52\" lines=\"128-142\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:183:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:184:Paint the maze corridor and framed rooms lying on shortest paths between the two colored endpoint components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:185:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:186:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:187:- The grid has a dominant background, one wall color forming thin orthogonal frames, and one endpoint/fill color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:188:- The endpoint/fill color forms exactly two 4-connected solid rectangular components; their larger side lengths define the framed room sizes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:189:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:190:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:191:- Treat wall pixels as blocked and every other pixel as passable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:192:- Find every passable pixel that lies on a shortest 4-connected path between the two endpoint components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:193:- Also fill any framed square room of an endpoint-derived size that intersects that shortest-path mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:194:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:195:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:196:- Shortest paths identify the route through open connector corridors, while the wall-bordered square rooms need to be expanded from the route centerline to their full interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:197:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:198:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:199:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:200:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8f215267\" lines=\"7-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:201:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:202:Count same-color patterns per frame and represent the tally as dots inside.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:203:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:204:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:205:- bg = most common color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:206:- Hollow rectangular frames in various colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:207:- Small monochrome pattern sprites scattered outside frames.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:208:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:209:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:210:- Remove all small patterns from the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:211:- For each frame of color C, count how many patterns share color C.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:212:- Draw that many dots along the frame's center row, spaced by 2, starting from the right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:213:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:214:Key insight: Frames act as tally displays — scattered same-color patterns are \"absorbed\" and their count is shown as interior dots.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:215:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:216:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:217:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:218:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9caf5b84\" lines=\"28-45\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:219:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:220:Recolor every pixel whose color is not one of the two most frequent input colors to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:221:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:222:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:223:- The grid contains at least three colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:224:- Orange is absent from the input and is used only as the output replacement color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:225:- Exactly two colors occupy the top two frequency ranks; they may tie with each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:226:  other, but no third color ties them at the cutoff.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:227:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:228:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:229:- Preserve every pixel whose color is one of the two most frequent input colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:230:- Replace every other pixel with orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:231:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:232:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:233:- The visible distinction is not the numeric identity of the colors but their\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:234:  population: the two majority colors remain, while all minority colors merge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:235:  into the new orange color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:236:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:237:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:238:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:239:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"1efba499\" lines=\"70-85\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:240:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:241:Swap paired marker pixels across the largest foreground-color barrier, placing them just outside the barrier segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:242:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:243:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:244:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:245:- One foreground color is the unique most frequent non-background color; its pixels form the stationary barrier.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:246:- Other foreground pixels are single markers, sometimes paired on opposite sides of one contiguous barrier segment in the same row or column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:247:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:248:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:249:- Scan each row and column that crosses exactly one contiguous barrier segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:250:- If the line has exactly one marker on each side of that segment, erase both source markers and place each marker in the cell immediately beyond the opposite side of the segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:251:- Lines with markers on only one side are unchanged; the barrier remains unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:252:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:253:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:254:- The marker pairing is local to a row or column, and the destination is defined by the nearest cells outside the intervening barrier segment, not by the original distance from the barrier.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:255:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:256:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:257:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:258:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"cbebaa4b\" lines=\"51-65\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:259:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:260:Assemble scattered jigsaw sprites around a central yellow anchor by pairing red connector pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:261:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:262:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:263:- bg = black (0). Several colored sprites scattered on the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:264:- One anchor sprite contains a 3×3 yellow (4) block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:265:- Each sprite has red (2) connector pixels along its edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:266:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:267:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:268:- The anchor stays in place; remaining sprites attach one at a time.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:269:- Each sprite is translated so that one of its red pixels overlaps an unpaired red pixel on the growing assembly.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:270:- Every red connector must pair with exactly one other, forming a complete joined structure.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:271:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:272:Key insight: Red pixels act as jigsaw pegs — each must match exactly one counterpart, and the assembly order is determined by which unpaired connectors remain.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:273:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:274:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:275:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:276:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"edb79dae\" lines=\"39-53\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:277:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:278:Stamp recolored sprites into a framed region using placeholder positions and a color legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:279:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:280:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:281:- bg background, a rectangular single-color frame, colored placeholder cells inside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:282:- Outside the frame: sprite shapes (one per placeholder color) and a small legend mapping each placeholder color to an output color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:283:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:284:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:285:- Find the frame and its interior placeholders.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:286:- For each placeholder color, locate the matching-color sprite outside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:287:- Stamp each sprite at the placeholder's position inside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:288:- Recolor every stamped sprite to the output color defined by the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:289:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:290:Key insight: The legend pairs (overlapping two-color glyphs outside the frame) dictate the final recoloring — placeholder color selects the shape, legend maps it to the output color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:291:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:292:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:293:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:294:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dd6b8c4b\" lines=\"9-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:295:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:296:Move the closest reachable maroon pixels into the 3×3 block around the unique red center.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:297:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:298:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:299:- bg = orange floor, magenta walls, scattered maroon (9) pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:300:- A unique red (2) pixel marks the center of a 3×3 destination block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:301:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:302:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:303:- Maroon pixels connected to the destination through floor/maroon cells (not blocked by walls) are candidates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:304:- Rank candidates by distance to the destination; the closest ones fill the block in row-major order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:305:- Moved maroons are erased (replaced with floor color).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:306:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:307:Key insight: Wall barriers restrict connectivity — only maroon pixels reachable via flood-fill through the floor qualify, so proximity alone isn't enough.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:308:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:309:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:310:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:311:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"36a08778\" lines=\"8-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:312:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:313:Simulate water falling from top-edge sources, pooling on shelves, and cascading off edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:314:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:315:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:316:- bg = most common color; water = rarest non-bg; shelf = other non-bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:317:- Sources: water clusters touching top row. Shelves: horizontal segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:318:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:319:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:320:- Water falls down from sources, painting bg cells as water.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:321:- On hitting a shelf, it spreads across the shelf span plus one cell past each end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:322:- From those overflow positions, water resumes falling independently.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:323:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:324:Key insight: Each shelf splits a stream into two at its edges, creating a branching waterfall tree.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:325:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:326:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:327:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:328:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b745798f\" lines=\"18-33\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:329:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:330:Expand each 3-pixel L marker into a same-color corner L on an empty background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:331:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:332:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:333:- The grid is an odd square with one dominant background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:334:- Every foreground object is a monochromatic 4-connected 3-pixel L inside a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:335:  2x2 box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:336:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:337:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:338:- Clear the grid to the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:339:- For each marker, map its L orientation to the corresponding outer corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:340:  and draw that corner L in the marker color with arm length half the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:341:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:342:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:343:- The small marker is a miniature corner; its orientation, not its position,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:344:  chooses which outer corner receives the expanded L.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:345:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:346:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:347:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:348:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"28a6681f\" lines=\"8-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:349:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:350:Simulate water pixels falling under gravity into basins formed by colored obstacles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:351:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:352:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:353:- bg = 0. Water pixels = color 1 (blue).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:354:- Other colors form static solid structures (walls, steps, containers).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:355:- Water starts in unstable positions above or beside basins.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:356:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:357:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:358:- Each water pixel falls straight down through bg cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:359:- When blocked below, it slides diagonally through the unique open side cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:360:- When resting on a surface, it slides horizontally toward the nearest gap where it can fall again.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:361:- Process repeats until no water pixel moves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:362:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:363:Key insight: Water seeks the deepest reachable basin via diagonal and horizontal sliding, not just vertical fall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:364:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:365:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:366:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:367:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"21897d95\" lines=\"283-301\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:368:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:369:Repaint regions from T-shaped control markers, erase the markers, and optionally rotate based on a color-9 L-marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:370:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:371:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:372:- The grid is a mosaic of monochrome regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:373:- Color 1 forms T-shaped control markers on region boundaries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:374:- Some controls use three singleton color-1 pixels around a colored center; that center is a literal replacement color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:375:- An optional 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker triggers 90-degree rotation of the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:376:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:377:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:378:- For a color-1 T marker, the single stem points at the destination region to repaint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:379:- The two diagonal cells behind the stem identify the source region; the destination gets that source region's original color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:380:- For a colored-center T marker, the same stem identifies the destination, but the center color is the replacement.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:381:- All marker cells are filled with the final color of the source-side region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:382:- A 5-cell L-shaped color-9 marker controls rotation: ┐ (corner top-right) → CCW 90°, ┌ (corner top-left) → CW 90°.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:383:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:384:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:385:- The stem chooses what changes, while the two diagonals behind the stem choose where the marker itself belongs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:386:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:387:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:388:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:389:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:390:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:391:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:392:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:393:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:394:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:395:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:396:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:397:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:398:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:399:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:400:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:401:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:402:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:403:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:404:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:405:请一次性生成 5 个 `<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:406:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:407:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:408:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:409:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:410:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:411:   - **不建议使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算 / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:412:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id是不可用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:413:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:414:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:415:6. 5 个新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:416:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:417:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:418:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:419:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:420:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:421:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:422:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:423:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:424:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:425:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:426:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:427:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:428:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:429:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:430:3. 可实现性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:431:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:432:4. ARC 合规性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2/prompt.md:433:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
