{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'for f in /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/2/codegen_prompts/*; do echo FILE:$f; sed -n '\"'1,220p' \\\"\"'$f\"; break; done'","aggregated_output":"FILE:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/2/codegen_prompts/1.md\n你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/2`\n- 题号：`1`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/2/1.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"1\">\n- `description`：通过比较每个前景对象与其最近邻对象的边界接触面长度，将接触面较短的一方吸收合并到接触面较长的一方中。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干个 4-连通单色前景对象，每个对象使用不同颜色（如 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow 等）。\n  - 部分对象之间存在水平或垂直方向上恰好相隔一像素的间隙（即它们的边界之间有一列或一行的背景间隔）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每对间隔恰好一像素的相邻对象，计算它们在间隔方向上的共享边界长度（即对齐的行数或列数）。\n  - 在该对中，面积较小的对象被重新着色为面积较大对象的颜色，同时将两者之间的一像素间隙也填充为较大对象的颜色。\n  - 如果两对象面积相同，则保持两者不变，间隙也不填充。\n  - 没有一像素间隙邻居的对象保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：一像素间隙定义了哪些对象构成\"邻居对\"；面积比较决定合并方向；间隙被填充表明合并不仅是重着色，还包含空间连接。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/753ea09b, train/d93c6891, train/8dab14c2, train/78e78cff, train/8886d717, eval/332f06d7, train/538b439f, eval/221dfab4\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"753ea09b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3855\nmechanism=0.4613\nlexical=0.0163\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:recolor, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/753ea09b.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/753ea09b.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill the small background compartments bounded by the long contour color.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has one dominant background color and two foreground colors.\n- The more frequent foreground color forms long 8-connected contour fragments.\n- The other foreground color is a fixed distractor/obstacle color that partitions\n  the background but is never recolored.\n\nRule:\n- Split the background into 4-connected regions using all foreground pixels as\n  barriers.\n- Keep the two largest background regions as the outside of the contour drawing.\n- Recolor every other background region that touches a long contour component\n  to the contour color; leave all foreground pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\nThe apparent area fill is exactly a component-level fill of bounded background\ncompartments, not a row-wise interpolation between individual contour pixels.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected background regions partitioned by long 8-connected contour-color components and obstacle-color pixels\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor each non-exterior background region touching a long contour component to the contour color; keep the two largest background regions and all foreground pixels unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"d93c6891\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3626\nmechanism=0.4385\nlexical=0.0220\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:recolor, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d93c6891.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/d93c6891.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove each gray bar into its adjacent orange rectangle as full stripes from the contacted edge.\n\nInput structure\n- The scene uses black outside space, yellow fill, gray one-cell-thick bars, and solid orange rectangles.\n- Each gray bar 4-touches exactly one orange rectangle; some orange rectangles have no touching gray bar.\n- Gray bars touching the same orange rectangle all have the same orientation.\n\nRule\n- Recolor every original gray cell to yellow.\n- For each orange rectangle touched by gray bars, count the gray cells assigned to that rectangle.\n- Horizontal gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange rows starting from the contacted top or bottom row.\n- Vertical gray bars repaint that many cells as complete orange columns starting from the contacted left or right column.\n- Orange rectangles with no touching gray bar remain unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The gray pixels are not copied by shape; their count is transferred into the neighboring orange rectangle as edge-aligned row or column stripes.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"gray one-cell-thick bars s\",\n  \"dst\": \"4-adjacent solid orange rectangles d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s 4-touches d\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase s to yellow; in each matched d, repaint |matched s cells| orange cells gray as complete rows for horizontal bars or complete columns for vertical bars from the touched edge\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8dab14c2\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3178\nmechanism=0.3746\nlexical=0.0155\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:counter, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, relation:adjacent, relation:aligned, relation:between, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8dab14c2.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8dab14c2.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete each boundary tab or notch by adding the complementary feature on the opposite side of the foreground object.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has exactly two colors: a dominant background and one foreground object.\n- The foreground object is a thick rectilinear shape with one-pixel tabs and notches on its boundary.\n\nRule\n- A foreground tab is a one-neighbor boundary pixel; project through its full row or column span and remove the opposite edge pixel to make a matching notch.\n- A background notch is a one-pixel cut with three foreground 4-neighbors; project across the full row or column span and add a tab just outside the opposite edge.\n- Notches immediately beside a tab source are not independent sources, because that gap belongs to the tab's local boundary shape.\n\nKey insight\n- The changed pixels are not color-specific noise; they are paired jigsaw-like boundary features on opposite sides of the same thick row or column cross-section.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one thick monochrome foreground object on a dominant background, with one-pixel boundary tabs and missing edge pixels\",\n  \"transform\": \"for each foreground tab, remove the opposite edge pixel on the same row or column; for each missing edge pixel, add a foreground tab just outside the opposite edge, ignoring gaps immediately beside a tab source\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"78e78cff\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3275\nmechanism=0.4476\nlexical=0.0156\ncode_feature=0.1667\noverlap_tags=code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, operation:recolor, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:nearest, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/78e78cff.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/78e78cff.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor the row-wise passage indicated by wall pixels with the singleton marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one singleton marker pixel and one wall color.\n- Wall pixels lie on several rows and form left/right limits around the marker column.\n- Empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows are open horizontal passages.\n\nRule:\n- On a wall row, paint background pixels between the nearest wall strictly\n  left of the marker column and the nearest wall at or right of it; if only\n  one side is present, paint from that wall to the opposite grid edge.\n- On empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows, paint the whole row.\n- On empty rows outside the wall-row band, reuse the nearest end wall-row interval.\n- Preserve wall pixels and the original marker pixel.\n\nKey insight:\n- The wall color defines scanline limits relative to the marker column; the\n  marker color fills those implied horizontal spans rather than flood-filling\n  through connected background.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one singleton marker pixel and rows of wall-color pixels on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor background pixels in the scanline passage selected by the marker column: wall rows fill between nearest wall limits, empty interior rows fill full width, and empty exterior rows reuse the nearest end interval\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8886d717\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3135\nmechanism=0.3680\nlexical=0.0161\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:counter, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, operation:recolor, output:same_size, relation:adjacent, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8886d717.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8886d717.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRepair markers embedded in the main object and copy the remaining markers one pixel toward the solid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- A mostly background grid contains one solid non-background edge line.\n- Apart from that edge and the background, there is one large main object\n  color and a smaller marker color.\n- Each marker is either embedded in the main object, touching it on at\n  least three 4-neighbor sides, or isolated on the background.\n\nRule:\n- Embedded markers are recolored to the main object color.\n- Isolated background markers remain in place and also paint the adjacent\n  background pixel in the direction of the solid edge line.\n- All other pixels are unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
